{"id": "EUVD-2026-103513", "enisaUuid": "75496e9b-2fd9-3fba-9b37-e7cdcbb04b5d", "description": "Xinference through 4.0.1 contains a path traversal vulnerability on Windows that allows unauthenticated attackers to write and delete arbitrary .json files via backslash sequences in model_name. Attackers can register a persisted custom model through POST /v1/model_registrations/{model_type} with names like ..\\..\\evil to overwrite configuration or data files writable by the Xinference process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T12:19:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:38:08", "baseScore": 8.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/xorbitsai/inference/issues/5702", "https://github.com/xorbitsai/inference/commit/beddc97ac211f8414597fe8479493be0603f7c84", "https://github.com/xorbitsai/inference/blob/v4.0.1/xinference/model/utils.py#L1175-L1182", "https://github.com/xorbitsai/inference/blob/v4.0.1/xinference/model/cache_manager.py#L117-L134", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/xinference-through-4.0.1-path-traversal-via-model-name-in-custom-model-registration"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112051", "GHSA-xhc4-qrhj-p2jj"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.37, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e68c8e30-3f85-3540-a778-78f3c940af5d", "product": {"name": "Inference", "vendor": {"name": "Xorbits"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22644.0.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "54edefc8-1986-3bad-84ab-b5d86ad35a12", "vendor": {"name": "xorbitsai"}}], "isExploited": false}